# Kona console / CLI output (locked)

User-facing terminal output for `kona`, `./grind`, and any future CLI must use **Termwind-inspired** styling:

- Canonical type: `org.konaframework.support.console.ConsoleIO` (`kona-support`)
- grind: `org.konaframework.grind.GrindIO` (wraps `ConsoleIO` + quiet/verbose)
- Brand: primary `#FF9A00`, accent `#286291`
- Env: `NO_COLOR`, `FORCE_COLOR` (`0` = off), `TERM=dumb`

## Required

- Prefer `info` / `success` / `warn` / `error`, `title`, `box`, `twoColumn`, `progress`
- Keep `scripts/install.sh` visually aligned (ANSI on stderr)

## Forbidden

- Raw `println` / unstyled `System.out` / `System.err` for user-facing command output
- A second, ad-hoc color scheme in a new CLI module

See [docs/architecture/components.md](docs/architecture/components.md) § Console / CLI output.
